<main id="main">
<section class="sub-hero"><div class="sub-hero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/living-room.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/living-room-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/living-room.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="shell sub-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">›</span><span aria-current="page">Appraisal FAQ</span></nav><p class="kicker">Answers by topic</p><h1>Utah Insurance Appraisal FAQ</h1><p class="lede">Plain answers to the questions we hear most, grouped by topic: the basics, costs and timing, Utah-specific rules and working with us.</p><div class="row-btns"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-l" href="/contact-utah-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section><div class="shell two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="jump"><a href="#t-0">Appraisal basics</a><a href="#t-1">Costs and timing</a><a href="#t-2">Utah-specific questions</a><a href="#t-3">Working with us</a></div><h2 id="t-0">Appraisal basics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>A process in most property policies for resolving disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side picks an appraiser, the appraisers pick an umpire, and any two can sign a binding award on the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Who can demand appraisal?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Either you or the insurer, in writing, when you disagree on the amount of loss. Check your policy for any steps that must come first.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is the award binding?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>On the amount of loss, generally yes, once two of the three panel members sign. Courts can set awards aside in limited situations, such as fraud or a lack of impartiality.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does appraisal decide coverage?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>No. It decides how much the covered damage costs. Disputes about whether something is covered are handled separately.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="t-1">Costs and timing</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How much does an appraiser cost?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Fee arrangements vary. Some appraisers charge hourly, some a flat fee and some a percentage of the increase. Each side pays its own appraiser and usually half of the umpire. Get terms in writing.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long does appraisal take?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Many residential appraisals finish within two to four months of both appraisers being named. Complex commercial claims can take longer.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal cheaper than a lawsuit?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Usually it’s faster and less expensive, because it focuses only on the amount of loss and avoids formal litigation. It also decides less.</p></div></details><details><summary>When is a gap too small for appraisal?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>When fees would eat most of the expected increase. Our claim gap and fee estimator shows the math for your numbers.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="t-2">Utah-specific questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurance in Utah?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>The Utah Insurance Department, led by the insurance commissioner. It licenses insurers, adjusters and public adjusters and accepts consumer complaints.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Utah have a FAIR plan or wind pool?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Utah doesn’t operate a state FAIR plan or wind pool like some coastal states. Properties that standard carriers decline are typically placed in the surplus lines market. Ask your agent about options.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long do I have to sue my insurer in Utah?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Utah law generally allows three years from the inception of the loss for actions on first-party property policies. Confirm with a Utah attorney, especially if a deadline is close.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if I think my insurer acted in bad faith?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Utah generally treats an insurer’s duty of good faith to its own policyholder as part of the insurance contract, and the Insurance Code lists unfair claim settlement practices that the Insurance Department enforces. These are legal questions for a Utah attorney; appraisal doesn’t address them.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is earthquake damage covered in Utah?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Not under most standard homeowners policies. Earthquake coverage is usually an endorsement or separate policy with a percentage deductible.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="t-3">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do you work for the insurance company?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>When we serve as your appraiser, we’re retained by you. When we serve as an umpire, we’re neutral and represent neither side.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are you a public adjuster or law firm?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>No. We provide appraisal, estimating and umpire services. We don’t negotiate claims outside appraisal and don’t give legal advice.</p></div></details><details><summary>What areas of Utah do you serve?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>All 29 counties, from Cache Valley to Washington County, including mountain and rural properties.</p></div></details><details><summary>What should I send for a free review?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>The carrier’s full estimate, your declarations page, photos and any contractor estimate or correspondence.</p></div></details></div></article><aside class="aside"><div class="aside-in"><div class="side-box side-call"><h2 class="side-t">Talk it through, free</h2><p>Send the carrier’s estimate or call. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal is worth it.</p><a class="side-phone" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-accent btn-block" href="/contact-utah-appraiser/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="side-box"><h2 class="side-t">Resources</h2><ul class="side-links"><li><a href="/how-utah-appraisal-works/">How appraisal works<svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-faq/" aria-current="page">Appraisal FAQ<svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/claim-terms-glossary/">Claim terms glossary<svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/utah-claim-articles/">Claim articles<svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div><section class="cta-strip"><div class="shell cta-strip-in rv"><div><h2>Didn’t see your question?</h2><p>Call or email. We’re glad to talk it through.</p></div><div class="row-btns"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-l" href="/contact-utah-appraiser/">Send claim details</a></div></div></section>
